 behaviors.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775487870397","neuronKeys":["[#f645d]","[#fc577]","[#7da09]"],"edgeStrings":["[#f645d]_#_[#fc577]","[#fc577]_#_[#7da09]"],"description":"First, as long as there is a treat in front of SpikerBot’s mouth, it will stop barking and blinking at the sight of people.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775488069445","neuronKeys":["[#f645d]","[#1c768]","[#2734f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#f645d]_#_[#2734f]","[#f645d]_#_[#1c768]","[#2734f]_#_[#1c768]"],"description":"These 3 neurons will produce Feed Forward Inhibition, causing the output excitatory neuron in the bottom right to only fire once each time something is detected in front of the distance sensor. The object must be removed to retrigger the bottom right neuron again.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775488157992","neuronKeys":["[#1c768]","[#198ca]"],"edgeStrings":["[#1c768]_#_[#198ca]"],"description":"When the Feed Forward Inhibition triggers, we will send just one burst to the first delay neuron to kickstart an action","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775488252780","neuronKeys":["[#198ca]","[#f37bc]"],"edgeStrings":["[#f37bc]_#_[#198ca]","[#198ca]_#_[#f37bc]"],"description":"When we get this single burst, these delay neurons will send their signals back and forth back and forth with a short delay, triggering a left and right turnas SpikerBot licks your hand or eats the treat!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775488321465","neuronKeys":["[#95fb7]"],"edgeStrings":["[#95fb7]_#_[#f37bc]"],"description":"This inhibitory neuron wants to fire regularly, set to highly active. When it fires, it stops the back and forth behavior set by the delay neurons.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775488447753","neuronKeys":["[#f645d]","[#fc577]","[#95fb7]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b4aad]_#_[#f645d]","[#f645d]_#_[#fc577]","[#fc577]_#_[#95fb7]"],"description":"As long as Spikerbot senses something in front of it’s mouth, we stop the command that tells spikerbot to stop wiggling. But when we remove the object from in front of SpikerBot, we allow the final inhibitory neuron to shut down the activation of our movement.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Watchdog","description":"Simple Behavior that barks at people, but stops to eat when given a treat!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:30:41.491853"}}